      "text": "A root of $x^3 + 3x^2 + ax + 7 = 0$ occurs when $x^2 + 3x + a = 0.$  Thus, if the third root is $b,$ then $ab = -7.$  Because $a$ and $b$ are integers, $ab = -7$ has twelve integer solutions given by\n\\[(a,b) = (-7,-1), (-1,-7), (1,7), (-1,1), (7,-1), (1,-7), (-7,1), (-1,7), (7,-1), (-1,-7), (1,-1), \\text{and} \\ (1,1).\\]We conclude that all possible values of $a$ are $-7, -1, 1,$ and $7.$.",
